    "legal_review_status": "Reviewed 2026-08-10 via an AI legal-review pass (fable model, see BACKLOG.md DN-53 second-module entry), grounded in current GWB/StGB statute text and the three named enforcement sources. 17/20 questions confirmed accurate on first pass. Fixed 2 citation/wording defects that didn't change any answer key: kartellrecht-straftaten-04's legal_basis corrected from the wrong §81b GWB (association-fine liability) to §§81h ff. GWB (the actual Kronzeugenprogramm/Bonusregelung provisions); kartellrecht-selbstreinigung-03's claimed 'schriftlich' (written-form) requirement for §125 Abs. 2 GWB's reasons obligation removed - the statute does not in fact prescribe a specific form. Also fixed a garbled explanation sentence in kartellrecht-kernbeschraenkungen-03 (automotive-recycling cartel: manufacturers agreed among themselves not to advertise recyclability to customers, not 'to each other'). Still NOT reviewed by a licensed lawyer or Kartellrechts-Compliance-Beauftragter - that human-review gate remains before commercial/production use. Follow-up (2026-08-10): a second, independent fable-model pre-review-dossier pass re-verified all 20 citations with zero new substantive errors, but found 2 wording-precision issues (both fixed, no answer-key changes): kartellrecht-selbstreinigung-04 now distinguishes §123 GWB's mandatory exclusion grounds from §124 GWB's facultative ones (cartel offenses typically fall under the discretionary §124 ground, not an automatic §123 exclusion); kartellrecht-selbstreinigung-02 now describes training as part of the combined \"technical, organizational, and personnel measures\" requirement rather than implying a separate formal \"personnel measures\" category. Also corrected the module description's overclaim of Sec. 19 GWB / Art. 102 TFEU coverage (researched but no dedicated question exists yet - flagged for the next round). Full dossier: claude/kartellrecht-pre-review-dossier-2026-08-10.md (Claude Project).",
